1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:02,452
We're making good progress on this app.

2
00:00:02,661 --> 00:00:04,424
Obviously, the next step is to work on this

3
00:00:04,424 --> 00:00:07,053
authenticated area and add that rich text

4
00:00:07,085 --> 00:00:10,098
editor and allow users to create and manage

5
00:00:10,195 --> 00:00:12,776
their notes. But before we do that, I wanna

6
00:00:12,776 --> 00:00:15,645
dive into the important concept of working

7
00:00:15,741 --> 00:00:17,232
with agent skills.

8
00:00:17,985 --> 00:00:20,775
Because that is a feature supported by Codex

9
00:00:20,775 --> 00:00:23,259
and actually pretty much all coding

10
00:00:23,355 --> 00:00:24,942
assistants and AI agents

11
00:00:25,584 --> 00:00:28,533
that is all about overcoming the problem of

12
00:00:28,565 --> 00:00:31,258
the AI agent and the underlying AI models

13
00:00:31,354 --> 00:00:34,308
having limited knowledge about certain

14
00:00:34,484 --> 00:00:36,700
features you may be using in your code or

15
00:00:36,764 --> 00:00:39,125
certain patterns you want to use or certain

16
00:00:39,157 --> 00:00:41,485
third-party libraries. And they also may

17
00:00:41,485 --> 00:00:43,781
have been trained on bad patterns or in

18
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:46,671
general patterns or approaches you don't

19
00:00:46,703 --> 00:00:48,276
wanna use in your codebase.

20
00:00:48,854 --> 00:00:52,242
So they may be lacking some skills you want

21
00:00:52,242 --> 00:00:54,811
them to have. And therefore those agents may

22
00:00:54,811 --> 00:00:57,476
not write the code the way you want or they

23
00:00:57,476 --> 00:00:59,516
may just not know about certain libraries,

24
00:00:59,628 --> 00:01:01,569
patterns, et cetera. Now, of course, as we

25
00:01:01,569 --> 00:01:04,294
saw before, there are ways of fixing some of

26
00:01:04,294 --> 00:01:07,516
these problems. If you know that an agent or

27
00:01:07,645 --> 00:01:09,568
the AI model doesn't know enough about a

28
00:01:09,568 --> 00:01:10,947
certain library you'll use,

29
00:01:11,492 --> 00:01:14,185
you can manually bring in the extra context

30
00:01:14,281 --> 00:01:17,118
or use an MCP. Or you could, of course, also

31
00:01:17,247 --> 00:01:19,988
put all that extra information into AgentsMD

32
00:01:19,988 --> 00:01:22,280
because, as you learned, that will be loaded

33
00:01:22,777 --> 00:01:26,015
every time a new session starts. Now,

34
00:01:26,159 --> 00:01:28,404
putting it into AgentsMD is not a good idea

35
00:01:28,548 --> 00:01:30,119
though, and I'll get back to why in a

36
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:30,744
second.

37
00:01:31,273 --> 00:01:33,566
And relying on manually adding context or

38
00:01:33,694 --> 00:01:34,192
MCPs

39
00:01:34,721 --> 00:01:37,704
is a solution, but of course might not be

40
00:01:37,704 --> 00:01:40,608
super reliable. And for certain things like

41
00:01:40,672 --> 00:01:43,142
patterns you wanna use, there might not be

42
00:01:43,222 --> 00:01:45,403
any documentation that could be referenced.

43
00:01:45,644 --> 00:01:48,018
And that's the idea behind those skills. You

44
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:51,001
add extra skills, which are just files to

45
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:53,584
your project, to your coding agent. And

46
00:01:53,584 --> 00:01:56,118
those skills give the agent extra knowledge

47
00:01:56,294 --> 00:01:59,149
or even extra tools, extra scripts it may

48
00:01:59,502 --> 00:02:02,536
use and execute. And this entire idea of

49
00:02:02,713 --> 00:02:05,733
agent skills is actually standardized. And

50
00:02:06,006 --> 00:02:08,592
as mentioned, pretty much all AI agents,

51
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:11,130
even outside of coding, support this idea of

52
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:11,773
skills.

53
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:14,793
And a skill is really just a folder with a

54
00:02:14,793 --> 00:02:17,620
markdown file inside of it, a markdown file

55
00:02:17,652 --> 00:02:19,805
which has that extra information or these

56
00:02:19,981 --> 00:02:22,150
extra instructions you want to expose to

57
00:02:22,632 --> 00:02:25,411
your agent. You can then also add more

58
00:02:25,796 --> 00:02:28,093
subfolders and files, which may include

59
00:02:28,093 --> 00:02:30,576
scripts. That can be executed by the agent

60
00:02:30,995 --> 00:02:33,028
or extra references. If you have a more

61
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:36,223
detailed documentation you want
